WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
A lens controls the data surface. A permission policy controls who can receive that

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:12.707
lens. Both are JSON. In this example, an organization must be active and on a Pro plan

00:00:12.707 --> 00:00:18.873
before it receives the platform lens. Watch the policy and its evaluated decisions

00:00:18.873 --> 00:00:19.550
together.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:29.165
The all group requires every condition inside it. An attribute rule checks whether the

00:00:29.165 --> 00:00:34.997
customer relationship is active. A relationship rule follows the customer link and

00:00:34.997 --> 00:00:40.686
requires reader access. Roles can inherit actions: in this demo, an analyst also

00:00:40.686 --> 00:00:46.802
qualifies as a reader. These are executable rules, not instructions asking an agent to

00:00:46.802 --> 00:00:47.300
behave.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.616
Sofia can receive lenses from two providers. Her predicate asks for delayed shipments.

00:00:56.616 --> 00:01:02.229
The server checks the current catalog, validates the predicate within each selected

00:01:02.229 --> 00:01:07.911
lens, and translates the bounded queries through To Prisma. The answer contains only

00:01:07.911 --> 00:01:11.225
records returned through those authorized lenses.

00:01:14.725 --> 00:01:20.580
Now change Pacific from Pro to Starter. Its lens disappears from Sofia’s catalog. The

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.505
old request no longer has access to that lens. The workbench hides the earlier result.

00:01:26.505 --> 00:01:32.360
This is access revocation. Rule staleness is a different check: whether upstream lens

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:38.078
narrowing has made the predicate invalid. The new result includes only the provider

00:01:38.078 --> 00:01:39.524
she can still access.

00:01:43.024 --> 00:01:48.995
Try sending the old Pacific lens identifier again. The server rejects it because that

00:01:48.995 --> 00:01:54.965
lens is no longer available in this context. A saved query is not a saved permission.

00:01:54.965 --> 00:01:59.250
The current policy must still allow the request when it runs.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:09.000
We can narrow the customer policy to require the analyst action. Mateo is a viewer, so

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:15.251
the Andes lens is unavailable to him. Change his role to analyst, and that same policy

00:02:15.251 --> 00:02:21.357
allows it. The JSON stays visible while the engine evaluates changing attributes and

00:02:21.357 --> 00:02:22.375
relationships.
